11. Difference Between GROUP BY and PARTITION BY?
GROUP BY
Returns fewer rows.
 
SELECT DeptId,
 
       AVG(Salary)
 
FROM Employee
 
GROUP BY DeptId;
 
PARTITION BY
Keeps all rows.
 
SELECT Name,
 
       Salary,
 
       AVG(Salary)
 
       OVER(PARTITION BY DeptId)
 
FROM Employee;
 
PARTITION BY preserves detail rows. [DataEngine..._Interview | Word], [SQL_Interv..._Questions | Word]
12. How Do You Find the Nth Highest Salary?
Answer
 
WITH X AS
 
(
 
SELECT Salary,
 
ROW_NUMBER() OVER
 
(ORDER BY Salary DESC) rn
 
FROM Employee
 
)
 
SELECT Salary
 
FROM X
 
WHERE rn = 3;
 
Common interview question. [Interview...reparation | Word]
